# Backup encryption + alerting config, prod environment (docs/plans/prod-deploy.md §4 step 10,
# §6, Session 5/6 — the backup/monitoring scripts themselves aren't built yet, but this file's
# shape is fixed now so deploy-prod/make-prod-env.sh has somewhere to write the encryption key
# today). Lives ONLY on the VPS at /opt/ammari-prod/env/backup.env — never in this repo, never in
# GitHub.
#
# Deliberately does NOT duplicate S3_*: deploy-prod/backup/pg-backup.sh (Session 5) reads the S3
# credentials straight out of /opt/ammari-prod/env/admin.env instead — one bucket, one access key
# (docs/plans/prod-deploy.md §4 step 7, §9 "Later" list), not a second copy of the same secret.

# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48. Used by deploy-prod/backup/pg-backup.sh (Session 5) to
# AES-256 encrypt each nightly pg_dump before it ever leaves the VPS. LOSING THIS KEY MAKES EVERY
# EXISTING ENCRYPTED BACKUP PERMANENTLY UNREADABLE — there is no recovery path. Keep a copy in a
# password manager too, the moment it's generated, not just in this file
# (docs/plans/prod-deploy.md §6).
PG_BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Comma-separated recipient list for the backup-success and disk-space alert emails (Session 6,
# not yet built — sent via the prod Resend API key already in admin.env, no new credential
# needed). Confirmed recipients: the shop's own inbox and the owner's address
# (docs/plans/prod-deploy.md §6).
ALERT_EMAIL_TO=
